
The code is split to 4 parts:
  *SyntaxAnalysis   (flex, bison)
  *semantics        (semantic checks for each rule)
  *semantcs_ast     (semantic analysis with ast creation)
  *codegen          (final code generation after ir creation from ast)

In this README from onw on we will talk about codegen file
Note that the previous files are not fully up to date. the final one is codegen

the file settings.h is used for debugging pusrposes and can be used to enable printing functions
    - FLEX_DEBUG on/off for flex
        - specific debug options
    - HASHTBL_DEBUG on/off      -- shows contents of symbol table
        - specific debug options
    - AST_DEBUG on/off          -- generates image of ast 
    
    - IR_DEBUG                  -- prints ir code (quatruplets)

to compile  : make clean && make

to run      : ./gcpp <input.cpp>

output      : out.asm   -- contains assembly code --

